    "bounding box" : [ 87.667, 568.667, 508.333, 665.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0]",
    "content" : "Abstract. In this paper, we consider the set of partitions ped ( n ) which counts the number of partitions of n wherein the even parts are distinct (and the odd parts are unrestricted). Using an algorithm developed by Radu, we prove congruences modulo 192 which were conjectured by Nath [ Nat24 ]. Further, we prove a few inﬁnite families of congruences modulo 24 by using a result of Newman. Also, we prove that ped (9 n + 7) is lacunary modulo 2 k +2 · 3 and 3 k +1 · 4 for all positive integers k ≥ 0. We further prove an inﬁnite family of congruences for ped ( n ) modulo arbitrary powers of 2 by employing a result of Ono and Taguchi on the nilpotency of Hecke operators."
  }, {
